# Raw dumps of the private ops repo's scripts/ and tests/, staged here for the
# migration in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-11-ops-scripts-migration.md. This
# fork is PUBLIC and these are NOT cleared for it: the owner ruled the whole
# client-switcher workstream stays off the fork, and oldTests/ carried a real
# third-party home-server IP (redacted in place, but the ruling stands either
# way). Ignored so a stray `git add -A` cannot publish 65 unreviewed files.
# The migration copies vetted files into scripts/ and tests/ deliberately, one
# at a time, behind that plan's audit gate — it never stages these directories.
#
# They are also REDUNDANT, not a last copy: TRUNK-SEED-HANDOFF.md §1 verified
# them byte-identical to ChrisMiho/turtle-tournament's `proper-setup` branch,
# a private repo still intact at D:\TurtleWow with a live remote. The dumps are
# in fact a strict SUBSET — §2 found two workstreams that live only on that
# repo's origin/main and appear in no dump at all. Committing these would
# preserve less than what is already preserved, at the cost of publishing:
#   - OldHandoffs/backups/pre-alive-world-*/.env — a REAL 18-char DB_PASS, not
#     a ${VAR} or __PLACEHOLDER__. Verified by assignment shape, value unread.
#   - a third party's CGNAT home-server address, in 4 files
#   - .ts.net / tailnet identifiers, in 3 more
/OldScripts/
/oldTests/
/OldHandoffs/

